@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_086.jpg)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Answers: Expanded Genetic Codes


@left


- An engineered tRNA-synthetase pair can assign a chosen codon to a noncanonical amino acid.
- Four-base codons can expand the coding vocabulary, but ribosome decoding, reading-frame shifts, and competing translation affect yield.
- Chemical groups can add a site-specific label, crosslink, or handle for capture and purification.


@top-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_086.jpg)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_087.jpg)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Answers: Expanded Genetic Codes - Applications


@left


- Site-specific labeling can help track proteins or test molecular interactions.
- Crosslinking residues can capture transient contacts; affinity handles can simplify purification.
- Every engineered system needs controls for incorporation efficiency, fidelity, cell growth, and protein function.


@top-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_087.jpg)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_088.jpg)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Answers: Four-Base Codons and Expanded Genetic Codes - Expand the translation code


@left


- A codon normally uses three RNA bases and is read by a matching transfer RNA during translation.
- An expanded code introduces a decoding rule so a chosen codon can direct a noncanonical amino acid.
- Quadruplet codons use four-base signals, but decoding must avoid competition with natural translation.


@top-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_088.jpg)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_085.jpg)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Answers: Four-Base Codons and Expanded Genetic Codes - Install a noncanonical amino acid


@left


- An orthogonal transfer-RNA and aminoacyl-tRNA synthetase pair can recognize a selected codon and charge a chosen amino acid.
- The engineered components should interact minimally with the host's native tRNAs and synthetases.
- Expression conditions and amino-acid availability affect incorporation efficiency.


@top-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_085.jpg)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to expanded codons](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_086.jpg)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Answers: Four-Base Codons and Expanded Genetic Codes - Use and verify new chemistry


@left


- Noncanonical residues can add handles for labeling, cross-linking, selective conjugation, or new catalytic chemistry.
- Confirm site-specific incorporation and full-length product, then test folding, activity, and purity.
- Codon reassignment can be incomplete or context-dependent, so analytical verification is essential.


